From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Carney <tim.carney@cargt.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:22:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 35/36] arm64: dts: imx93-cargt-00324: mux WDOG_ANY for the
 wdog3 board reset

The 00324 SOM wires the WDOG_ANY pad (MPU_WDOG_B) through R32 to the
PCA9451's WDOG_B input, like NXP's i.MX93 EVK. Mux the pad in the SOM
dtsi and state fsl,ext-reset-output on wdog3 there, so every 00324
carrier gets the watchdog board reset. Drop the 00326 dts's own wdog3
status = "okay", which the SOM now covers.

NXP's lf-6.6 imx93.dtsi already sets fsl,ext-reset-output on wdog3, so
here this mainly makes the pad mux explicit rather than relying on its
reset default. On wrynose (6.18) the SoC dtsi no longer sets the
property, and a wdog3 timeout only wrapped the counter without
resetting the board. This keeps scarthgap's board DT the same as
wrynose's.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board specific]
---
 .../dts/freescale/imx93-cargt-00324-00326.dts |  4 ----
 .../boot/dts/freescale/imx93-cargt-00324.dtsi | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx93-cargt-00324-00326.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx93-cargt-00324-00326.dts
index b7eae16f0668..907121611b5d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx93-cargt-00324-00326.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx93-cargt-00324-00326.dts
@@ -86,10 +86,6 @@ aliases {
 	 };
  };
 
- &wdog3 {
-	status = "okay";
- };
- 
  &flexcan1 {
 	 pinctrl-names = "default";
 	 pinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_flexcan1>;
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx93-cargt-00324.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx93-cargt-00324.dtsi
index c4cd59d35953..61de349d649c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx93-cargt-00324.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx93-cargt-00324.dtsi
@@ -258,6 +258,19 @@ &usdhc1 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * The SOM wires WDOG_ANY (MPU_WDOG_B) through R32 to the PMIC's WDOG_B
+ * input, as on NXP's i.MX93 EVK. Without fsl,ext-reset-output the
+ * imx7ulp driver leaves CS[INT]=0 and a wdog3 timeout only wraps the
+ * counter instead of resetting the board.
+ */
+&wdog3 {
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_wdog>;
+	fsl,ext-reset-output;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &iomuxc {
 	pinctrl_eqos: eqosgrp {
 		fsl,pins = <
@@ -331,6 +344,12 @@ MX93_PAD_SD1_STROBE__USDHC1_STROBE	0x15fe
 		>;
 	};
 
+	pinctrl_wdog: wdoggrp {
+		fsl,pins = <
+			MX93_PAD_WDOG_ANY__WDOG1_WDOG_ANY	0x31e
+		>;
+	};
+
 };
 
 &epxp {
